      text: `<p>Let A be&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>3</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> real matrix such that its characteristic equation is given by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&lambda;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">&lambda;</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&ndash;</mo><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">&lambda;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">&lambda;</mi><mo>&ndash;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, which of the following statements is necessarily true?</p>`,
