      text: `<p>Let A be a singular&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> matrix with eigen vectors<em> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></em>&nbsp;for <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>&nbsp;and <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, respectively. If&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>, the system <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math>:</p>`,
