      answer: "B",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4a676e5b979df24335d29&questionId=6a26ba37cb63bfb96e5a000c&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4a676e5b979df24335d29&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a26ba37cb63bfb96e5a000c&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F60784791-698b-4793-bab7-0803afb988e7%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a26ba37cb63bfb96e5a000d&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:47)</a></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open="[" close="]"><mtable columnalign="left" equalrows="true" equalcolumns="true"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>
<p>b lies in column space of A, which means the system is consistent (i.e. either the system has unique solution or infinitely many solutions)</p>
<p>Now,&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math></span> A is singular <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> </span>det(A) = 0</p>
<p>&nbsp;<span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;...(1)</p>
<p>By rank-nullity theorem:</p>
<p><span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></span> + Nullity(A) = n</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> 3 &times; 3 matrix <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math></span> n = 3</p>
<p>Nullity(A) = n &ndash; <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></span>&nbsp;= 3 &ndash; <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math></span>From equation(1), Nullity&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and Nullity <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p><span style="font-family: symbol;">&nbsp;</span>We will get infinitely many solutions</p>
<p><strong>Concept summary</strong></p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 58.9636%;" border="1">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;"><strong>Condition</strong></td>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;"><strong>Solution type</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8713;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;">No solution (Inconsistent)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, Nullity = 0&nbsp;</td>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;">Unique solution</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, Nullity <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</td>
<td style="width: 50.0701%;">Infinitely many solution</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>So, option (b) is correct</p>`
