      text: `<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>X</mi></math> be a random variable following a normal distribution with mean <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&mu;</mi></math> and variance <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">&sigma;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, denoted as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>&sim;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&mu;</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">&sigma;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>
<p>We define a new random variable Y&nbsp;as:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">Y</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <msup> <mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&mu;</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <msup><mi mathvariant="normal">&sigma;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup> </mfrac> </mrow> </math></p>
<p>If the probability <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Y</mi><mo>&le;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9544</mn></math>, what is the value of the constant <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></math>? [nearest integer value]</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 4,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4a6da6fcaa08f535c22f5&questionId=6a2ab15611097af99c1fd9ad&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4a6da6fcaa08f535c22f5&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a2ab15611097af99c1fd9ad&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F2bbea2fe-e439-4be8-a7e0-9bb7694a9e7d%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a2ab15611097af99c1fd9ae&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:00)</a></p>
<p>1. Transform to standard Normal:</p>
<p>Let <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&mu;</mi></mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">&sigma;</mi> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> since <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi> <mo>&sim;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi> <mo>(</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">&mu;</mi> <mo>,</mo> <msup><mi mathvariant="normal">&sigma;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup> <mo>)</mo> </mrow> </math>,</p>
<p>we have <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi> <mo>&sim;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">N</mi> <mo>(</mo> <mn>0</mn> <mo>,</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>)</mo> </mrow> </math></p>
<p>The variable&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>Y</mi></math> simplifies to</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">Y</mi> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mo>(</mo> <mfrac> <mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&mu;</mi></mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">&sigma;</mi> </mfrac> <mo>)</mo> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup> </mrow> </math></p>
<p>2. Relate to the Interval:</p>
<p>The condition <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi> <mo>(</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">Y</mi> <mo>&le;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi> <mo>)</mo> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0.9544</mn> </mrow> </math> is equivalent to</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi> <mo>(</mo> <msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup> <mo>&le;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi> <mo>)</mo> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0.9544</mn> </mrow> </math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi> <mo>(</mo> <mo>-</mo> <msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi></msqrt> <mo>&le;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi> <mo>&le;</mo> <msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi></msqrt> <mo>)</mo> <mo>=</mo> <mn>0.9544</mn> </mrow> </math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mo>∵</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi> <mo>(</mo> <mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn> <mo>&le;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi> <mo>&le;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>)</mo> <mo>≃</mo> <mn>0.6826</mn> </mrow> </math></p>
<p>and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi> <mo>(</mo> <mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn> <mo>&le;</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi> <mo>&le;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>)</mo> <mo>≃</mo> <mn>0.9544</mn> </mrow> </math></p>
<p>By comparing, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mrow> <msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi></msqrt> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>&rArr;</mo> <menclose notation="box"> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </menclose> </mrow> </math></p>`
