      video: "https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4a901986809213f5ba4fd&questionId=6a3be58ba3d27e0e35f630ba&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4a901986809213f5ba4fd&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a3be58ba3d27e0e35f630ba&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fbab10db0-b725-4b65-831c-9df61e5fd8e0%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a3be58ba3d27e0e35f630bb&back_button=false",
      text: `<p>A data file contains 10,000 records stored in 100 blocks. A sparse primary index and a dense primary index are built on the file. Let x denote the number of entries in the sparse index and y denote the number of entries in the dense index. The value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi></math> is ________.</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 10100,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4a901986809213f5ba4fd&questionId=6a3be58ba3d27e0e35f630ba&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4a901986809213f5ba4fd&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a3be58ba3d27e0e35f630ba&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fbab10db0-b725-4b65-831c-9df61e5fd8e0%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a3be58ba3d27e0e35f630bb&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:24)</a></p>
<p>In a sparse primary index, one index entry is maintained per data block.</p>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>In a dense index, one index entry is maintained per record.</p>
<p>Therefore,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Hence,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10100</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Therefore the answer is 10100.</p>`
