      text: `<p>In CRC , g(x) be the generator polynomial. Choose all the properties of a Good Generator polynomial?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>A good polynomial must have more than 1 term and coefficient of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math><sup> </sup>must be 1.</p>`,
        `<p>Generator polynomial must have a factor <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
        `<p>Generator polynomial must not divide <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
        `<p>If g(x) is a primitive polynomial of degree m, it can detect all double-bit errors provided the total frame length (including CRC bits) does not exceed <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>`,
      ],
