      marks: 2,
      neg: 0,
      type: "NAT",
      video: "https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ac36986809213f5c1422&questionId=6a4f7ea49bd8cd177b35420c&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ac36986809213f5c1422&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a4f7ea49bd8cd177b35420c&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F98793d41-4ca2-42b1-93ac-5bff1e173868%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a4f7ea49bd8cd177b35420d&back_button=false",
      text: `<p>Consider a system with 5 processes P1, P2, P3, P4, and P5. The system has 6 types of resources R1, R2, R3, R4, R5 and R6. Each resource has exactly one instance. Further consider the following resource allocation graph for the system:</p>
<p><img title="12.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/a7862f67-3e29-47d1-a233-8eb12be5e526.png" alt="" width="305" height="205" /></p>
<p>The number of processes which have at least one resource allocated, as per the above graph is _______?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        ``,
        ``,
        ``,
        ``,
      ],
      answer: 3,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ac36986809213f5c1422&questionId=6a4f7ea49bd8cd177b35420c&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ac36986809213f5c1422&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a4f7ea49bd8cd177b35420c&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F98793d41-4ca2-42b1-93ac-5bff1e173868%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a4f7ea49bd8cd177b35420d&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:19)</a></p>
<p>In the resource allocation graph, there are 2 types of edges:</p>
<p><strong>1.&nbsp; Allocation Edge: </strong>It shows which resource is allocated to which process and it is drawn from resource to process.</p>
<p><strong>2.&nbsp; Request Edge: </strong>It shows which process requested for which resource. And it is drawn from process to resource.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">In the given graph P1 process does not have any incoming edge, hence it does not have any allocated resource. And process P2 also does not have any incoming edge, hence it also does not have any allocated resource.</p>
<p>Remaining three processes P3, P4 and P5 are having resource allocated.</p>`
