      text: `<p>If G is a connected simple graph on n vertices, what is the minimum possible number of edges in G?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>n&minus;2</p>`,
        `<p>n&ndash;1</p>`,
        `<p>n</p>`,
        `<p>None of the above</p>`,
      ],
      answer: "B",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ad16905d3d6a8a2a5bb7&questionId=6a54a87afdcce2e3776e1c34&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ad16905d3d6a8a2a5bb7&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a54a87afdcce2e3776e1c34&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fd9b843a7-5391-4877-9887-c30112b09964%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a54a87afdcce2e3776e1c35&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:00:40)</a></p>
<p>A connected graph must have a path between every pair of vertices. The connected simple graphs with the fewest edges are trees. A fundamental result in graph theory states that:<br /><br />Every tree with n vertices has exactly n-1 edges.<br />Any connected graph with fewer than n-1 edges must be disconnected.<br /><br />Therefore, the minimum number of edges in a connected simple graph on n vertices is n-1.</p>`
