      text: `<p>A relation between two no. is as given below:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi></msub></math> minimum value of&nbsp; y for which this relation will be true is ______ .</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 23,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4aec1986809213f5d0146&questionId=6a62ed91a4846bdbf8a60ac7&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4aec1986809213f5d0146&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a62ed91a4846bdbf8a60ac7&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F3e046793-4b86-4f35-9e9c-4f3d79e81690%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a62ed91a4846bdbf8a60ac8&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:05:00)</a></p>
<p>Given</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi></msub></math></p>
<p>So for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>49</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi></msub></math> to be correct number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>10</mn></math> &amp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mfenced><mn>23</mn></mfenced><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi></msub></math> to be correct number <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>
<p>&amp; for&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mfenced><mn>49</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mfenced><mn>23</mn></mfenced><mi>y</mi></msub></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>10</mn></msub></math></p>
<p>y = (2x + 3)</p>
<p>so, for valid values for&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p>
<p>y will be 23, 25, 27, 29...</p>
<p>so (y) min = 23.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>`
