      text: `<p>A signed no. is given as (1011)<sub>2</sub> .</p>
<p>If this no. is represented in sign magnitude method then its decimal equivalent is given by x.</p>
<p>If this no. is represented in 1's compliment method then its decimal equivalent is given by y.</p>
<p>If this no. is represented in 2's compliment method then its decimal equivalent is given by z.</p>
<p>Then which of the following operations results into an overflow if result is expressed in 2's compliment representation.</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>x + z</p>`,
        `<p>y + z</p>`,
        `<p>&ndash; x &ndash; z</p>`,
        `<p>x + y</p>`,
      ],
      answer: ["B", "C"],
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4aec1986809213f5d0146&questionId=6a62ed91a4846bdbf8a60ad6&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4aec1986809213f5d0146&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a62ed91a4846bdbf8a60ad6&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F23d472ec-189d-4fa9-b5aa-83723d612f82%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a62ed91a4846bdbf8a60ad7&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:55)</a></p>
<p>x = 1011 = &ndash; 3 in sign magnitude method.</p>
<p>y = 1011 = &ndash; 4 in 1's &nbsp;compliment method.</p>
<p>z = 1011 = &ndash; 5 in 2s compliment method.</p>
<p>Now Range of no. in 2's compliment method from 4 bit is&nbsp;</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&minus;</mo><mo>(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo><mtext>&nbsp;to&nbsp;</mtext><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>&ndash; 8 to 7.</p>
<p>Now,</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext>&nbsp;&nbsp;No&nbsp;overflow.</mtext></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">z</mi><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>9</mn><mtext>&nbsp;overflow</mtext></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&minus;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">z</mi><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&rarr;</mo><mtext>&nbsp;overflow</mtext></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>7</mn><mtext>&nbsp;No&nbsp;overflow.</mtext></math></p>`
