      text: `<p>Consider the following array is declared &nbsp;&nbsp;<br />int A[ ] = {3,6,8,2,87, 54, 26, 76}&nbsp;<br />Suppose the base address of the array is 1000 and each element occupies 4 Bytes of space.&nbsp;<br />Consider the following function &nbsp;<br />void foo(int arr[], int start, int end) <br />&nbsp; {&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;while (start &lt; end) <br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;{&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; int temp = arr[start];&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; arr[start] = arr[end];&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; arr[end] = temp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; start++;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; end--;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;}&nbsp;<br />If we call the function as foo(A, 2,7), the address of element 2 is ___________?</p>`,
