      answer: "A",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4b0b60897516718e830eb&questionId=6a69a68fb4bd3bcec615662d&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4b0b60897516718e830eb&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a69a68fb4bd3bcec615662d&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fdf99c62c-9460-4354-8a38-27d8ce0e3b67%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a69a68fb4bd3bcec615662e&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:00:54)</a></p>
<p>Both P and Q<sub>&nbsp;</sub>are decidable. A DFA <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> accepts a string &ldquo;w&rdquo; is decidable and an NFA <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> rejects an string is also decidable, as we can convert NFA <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;into equivalent DFA and then we can decide that DFA rejects the string or not.</p>`
