      text: `<p>The girth of a graph is the length of its shortest cycle. Which one of the following options correctly gives the girths of the graphs&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">K</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Q</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>, and the Petersen graph respectively?</p>`,
