      answer: 64,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4b2ff6fcaa08f535c2ccf&questionId=6a795c2b4628a33852759797&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4b2ff6fcaa08f535c2ccf&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a795c2b4628a33852759797&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F454fbae9-6165-49c2-9ab4-abafb3df4385%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a795c2b4628a33852759798&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:02:39)</a></p>
<p>Number of chips<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>Total&#160;capacity</mtext><mtext>One&#160;chip&#160;capacity</mtext></mfrac></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>512</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mtext>&#160;bits</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mtext>&#160;bits</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math></p>
<p>= 64</p>`
