      text: `<p>Consider the standard Merge Sort algorithm used to sort an array containing 32 distinct elements.</p>
<p>Determine the total number of times the merge() function is invoked during the complete execution of the algorithm.</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        ``,
        ``,
        ``,
        ``,
      ],
      answer: 31,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&questionId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7f0&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7f0&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fd09d854e-4692-45bb-9be7-b74d62c1ecb6%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7f1&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:08:57)</a></p>
<p>Merge Sort recursively divides the array until each subarray contains exactly one element. The recursion tree therefore contains 32 leaf nodes, each representing a subarray of size 1.</p>
<p>A call to the merge() function occurs at every internal node of the recursion tree to merge the two sorted child subarrays.</p>
<p>A full binary tree with n leaf nodes has exactly n-1 internal nodes.</p>
<p>Hence, the total number of merge() function calls is</p>
<p>= 32-1</p>
<p>=31</p>
<p>Therefore, the merge() function is invoked 31 times.</p>`
