      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&questionId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7c4&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7c4&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F3fd46927-3c5c-4743-a524-fc8f84f48567%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7c5&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:27)</a></p>
<p>Let assume fun(n) taking time T(n) and inside fun(n) code there is two recursive function call of fun(n/2) and one for loop is there which takes <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> time. Hence, the running time satisfies the recurrence&nbsp;</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>The recursion depth is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p>Since each recursive call performs&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> work apart from the recursive call itself, the total running time is (nlog n).</p>
<p>Hence, the correct answer is (D).</p>`
