      text: `<p>Suppose only&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> units of time are available for sorting using Merge Sort. Approximately how many elements can be sorted within the available time?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>logn</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
        `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
        `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>`,
        `<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></msqrt></math></p>`,
      ],
      answer: "C",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&questionId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7dd&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7dd&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F2e1e9143-18c1-4b98-ab88-e9dcaa5aeb1a%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea7de&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:05:54)</a></p>
<p>Let m be the number of elements that can be sorted in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> time.</p>
<p>Since Merge Sort requires&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>)</mo></math> time,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Assume&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&times;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p>
<p>Therefore, approximately&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> elements can be sorted within&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">&Theta;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo></math> time.</p>
<p>Hence, the correct answer is (C).</p>`
