      text: `<p>Five sorted arrays A, B, C, D, and E contain 40, 18, 45, 27, and 22 elements, respectively. They are to be merged into a single sorted array by repeatedly merging exactly two arrays at a time. An optimal merging strategy is used. Assuming that each merge is performed in the best case, what is the minimum total number of comparisons required?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        ``,
        ``,
        ``,
        ``,
      ],
      answer: 152,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&questionId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea818&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4e5ea8180c1555cab2da8&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea818&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fc6df7759-1496-443d-b432-bf9fdef25979%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a842b5ca3d58651e9bea819&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:07:34)</a></p>
<p>The optimal strategy is to repeatedly merge the two smallest arrays.</p>
<p>Merge arrays of sizes 18 and 22 to obtain an array of size 40. Comparisons =18.</p>
<p>Merge arrays of sizes 27 and 40 to obtain an array of size 67. Comparisons =27.</p>
<p>Merge arrays of sizes 40 and 45 to obtain an array of size 85. Comparisons =40.</p>
<p>Finally, merge arrays of sizes 67 and 85. Comparisons =67.</p>
<p>Hence, the minimum total number of comparisons required is</p>
<p>18+27+40+67=152.</p>
<p>Therefore, the correct answer is 152.</p>`
