      text: `<p>Consider the following schedules</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mn>1</mn></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">w</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p>
<p>The number of schedules that are recoverable is ________.</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 0,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4e718502ee71a214baed6&questionId=6a8c247da6032413702baccb&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4e718502ee71a214baed6&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a8c247da6032413702baccb&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F39d133a3-fb16-4556-b5fb-21cec86f182f%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a8c247da6032413702baccc&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:34)</a></p>
<p>S1:</p>
<p>T2 reads from T1.</p>
<p>For recoverability, T1 must commit before T2.</p>
<p>But the commits are:</p>
<p>c2 ; c1</p>
<p>i.e., T2 commits before T1, which violates recoverability.</p>
<p>Thus, S1 is NOT recoverable.</p>
<p>S2:</p>
<p>r1(x) occurs after w2(x), so T1 reads the value written by T2.</p>
<p>Thus,</p>
<p>T1 reads from T2.</p>
<p>For recoverability, T2 must commit before T1.</p>
<p>But commits are:</p>
<p>c1 ; c2</p>
<p>So T1 commits before T2, which violates recoverability.</p>
<p>Thus, S2 is NOT recoverable.</p>`
