      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4e82d0897516718e86300&questionId=6a9250ad31b13144266630af&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4e82d0897516718e86300&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a9250ad31b13144266630af&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F1888efe9-6a14-42a0-9d5c-600db028426c%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a9250ad31b13144266630b0&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:06:44)</a></p>
<p>The subnet <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>21</mn></math> covers the address range&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>255</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;<br />Hence, the destination address <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math> matches both <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math><br />By the longest prefix match rule, the /21 entry is selected. Therefore, the next hop is P.&nbsp;<br />The subnet <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn></math> covers the address range&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>255</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math><br />Hence, the destination address <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>200</mn></math> matches both <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>172</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;<br />By the longest prefix match rule, the /24 entry is selected. Therefore, the next hop is Q.&nbsp;<br />Hence, the correct answer is (D).&nbsp;</p>`
