      answer: ["B", "D"],
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ee120897516718e866a5&questionId=6a969f22efd299bb977e96c8&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ee120897516718e866a5&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a969f22efd299bb977e96c8&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F400ff6b5-dd3a-4706-a7ca-ff4c09301410%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a969f22efd299bb977e96c9&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:16:37)</a></p>
<p>Initial semaphore values:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p>Also, initially only one of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8203;</mo></math> can execute because <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and remaining all semaphores are zero.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Hence the sequence can be started with either A or D.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Assuming if T1 executes wait(S1) successfully and prints A then T3 will have to wait until the signal(S1). Now T1 will execute signal (S2), but And T1 will have to wait until signal(S3). Which means either T2 or T5 can execute wait(S2) successfully and can print either C or B.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">So option C is not possible.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Let us assume T2 executes wait(S2) successfully then T2 prints C. T2 then executes signal(S3). After that T2 will wait for Signal(S1).</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">After that only T1 can execute wait(S3) and can print F.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">So in sequence A C F printed. Now T1 can execute signal (S4) and then T4 only can proceed and can print E. Hence option A is not possible.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">But option D is possible because after printing E T4 can execution signal(S1) and signal(S2). Hence T2 can execute wait(S1) print("G") signal(S1). And the further other all characters can be printed.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">If initially T3 starts and executes wait(S1) print("D") signal(S4). Then only T4 can proceed further and execute wait(S4) print("E") signal(S1) signal(S2). Now T5 can execute completely and can print B, J in sequence. Also T5 execute signal on S3, S4 and S2. Now T2 can fully execute and can print C, G. And then rest of the characters also can be printed in given sequence in option B.</p>`
