      text: `<p>Consider a disk which has <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> number of pending requests in some order to fulfil.&nbsp; Which of the following statements is correct for disk scheduling algorithm for the disk?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p style="text-align: justify;">Shortest seek time first (SSTF) algorithm always takes minimum number of head movements in servicing all pending requests</p>`,
        `<p style="text-align: justify;">Look algorithm always takes minimum number of head movements in servicing all pending requests</p>`,
        `<p style="text-align: justify;">Scan algorithm always takes minimum number of head movements in servicing all pending requests</p>`,
        `<p>None</p>`,
      ],
      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ee120897516718e866a5&questionId=6a969f22efd299bb977e96c5&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ee120897516718e866a5&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a969f22efd299bb977e96c5&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F910d7283-75a4-4625-8823-98528ad6f632%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a969f22efd299bb977e96c6&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:13:23)</a></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">In some scenarios SSTF can provide minimum head movements and in some scenarios Look algorithm also can provide minimum. So it cannot be said that always either of them will provide minimum head movements always.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Case 1:</strong> Where SSTF gives less number of head movements</p>
<p>Total number of cylinders 100 (0 to 99). Current head position at 50. 5 pending requests are for cylinder number 45, 42, 40, 60, 90. The disk head is moving towards larger number cylinder side.</p>
<ol>
<li>SSTF: 50<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>45<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>42<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>40<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>60<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>90</li>
<li>Look: 50<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>60<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>90 <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>45<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>42<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>40</li>
<li>Scan: 50<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>60<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>90<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>99<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>45<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>42<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>40</li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;Total head movements in SSTF, look and scan algorithms are 60, 90, and 108 respectively.</p>
<p><strong>Case 2: </strong>Where Look gives less number of head movements</p>
<p>Total number of cylinders 100 (0 to 99). Current head position at 50. 5 pending requests are for cylinder number 35, 20, 5, 66, 68. The disk head is moving towards larger number cylinder side.</p>
<ol>
<li>SSTF: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>68</mn></math></li>
<li>Look: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>68</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></li>
<li>Scan: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>68</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;Total head movements in SSTF, look and scan algorithms are 108, 81, and 143 respectively.</p>`
