      text: `<p>A logic circuit is designed as shown:</p>
<p>A, B &amp; C are inputs and y is output:</p>
<p><img title="1.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/a6087de5-348b-407b-846d-79484400ce6c.png" alt="" width="296" height="143" /></p>
<p>Then which of the following is/are true ?&nbsp;</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>Output y is &lsquo;1&rsquo; when majority inputs will be &lsquo;1&rsquo;.</p>`,
        `<p>Output y is &lsquo;0&rsquo; when majority inputs will be &lsquo;0&rsquo;.</p>`,
        `<p>Output y is &lsquo;1&rsquo; when odd no. of input lines are at logic &lsquo;1&rsquo;.</p>`,
        `<p>Output y is &lsquo;0&rsquo; when odd no. of input lines are at logic &lsquo;0&rsquo;.</p>`,
      ],
      answer: ["A", "B"],
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4eeff0897516718e866d3&questionId=6a9b960e6fe403fd33618fbc&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4eeff0897516718e866d3&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6a9b960e6fe403fd33618fbc&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fc3d68b05-ed0a-41ae-aa89-eca102c0f557%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6a9b960e6fe403fd33618fbd&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:02:02)</a></p>
<p>Lets draw the circuit and analyze it:</p>
<p><img title="1.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/6565205b-a186-4196-b69a-f78e0dd9c0c4.png" alt="" width="296" height="143" /></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math></p>
<p>= (A + B) (B + C) (C + A)</p>
<p>= AB + BC + CA</p>
<p>Output y is equivalent to carry output of full adder and thus output y will be '1' when majority input will be logic '1' and at the same time output y will be '0' when majority input will be '0' as when majority input will be at '0' then A.B, B.C &amp; C.A will definitely be '0'.</p>
<p>Hence (a, b) are correct options.</p>`
