      answer: ["A", "B"],
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4f15b1ab83565959d017c&questionId=6aae59134edeab974e8da1f6&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4f15b1ab83565959d017c&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6aae59134edeab974e8da1f6&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F81b16647-0cc0-469c-8926-546559ba1699%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6aae59134edeab974e8da1f7&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:03:00)</a></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi></msup><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;strings in L1={abc, abcc, abccc, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;..aabbc, aabbcc, aabbccc, &hellip;&hellip;..}</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></msup><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;strings in L2={abc, aabc, aaabc, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;, abbcc, aabbcc, aaabbcc,&hellip;&hellip;}</p>
<p>L1 and L2 both are DCFL.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8745;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;{abc, aabbcc, aaabbbccc, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;.} hence it is equal to L={a<sup>n</sup> b<sup>n</sup> c<sup>n</sup> | n&gt;0} which is CSL but not CFL.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8746;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;will be CFL as we cannot define push pop deterministically, hence it is CFL but not DCFL.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></munder><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8745;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></munder><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;will have strings such as { abbccc, aabccc, &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;} hence it is non empty language.</p>
<p>Since L1 and L2 are DCFL so they are CFL also and CFLs are closed under concatenation</p>
<p>So L1. L2 must be CFL.&nbsp;</p>`
