      text: `<p>Suppose a fictional calendar year has 600 days, with each week consisting of 9 days. How many odd days would there be in that calendar year?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>Two</p>`,
        `<p>Zero</p>`,
        `<p>Nine&nbsp;</p>`,
        `<p>Six</p>`,
      ],
      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4f1d5107980e9daa9c142&questionId=6ab249feeaa0977629d7c863&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4f1d5107980e9daa9c142&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6ab249feeaa0977629d7c863&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F650d82ab-e697-4ccf-875e-20bc95699e0a%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6ab249feeaa0977629d7c864&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:20)</a></p>
<p>A week has 9 days.</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>600</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>66</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p>
<p>So there are 66 complete weeks and 6 extra days.</p>
<p>Therefore, the number of odd days is: 6<br />&nbsp;​</p>`
