      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4f1d5107980e9daa9c142&questionId=6ab249feeaa0977629d7c8c2&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4f1d5107980e9daa9c142&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6ab249feeaa0977629d7c8c2&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fc3679641-0afe-45f3-b05d-a17f9cd6b579%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6ab249feeaa0977629d7c8c3&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:22)</a></p>
<p>The standard English structure is 'Hardly had ... when ...'. It is used to indicate that one event happened immediately after another. 'Than', 'then', and 'while' do not fit this grammatical construction.</p>`
