      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4f7903ac1a2e38d1834b7&questionId=6abfed72d13294cf8ca4c090&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4f7903ac1a2e38d1834b7&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6abfed72d13294cf8ca4c090&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F97111e9d-de3f-4343-865d-a25179c9f5bb%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6abfed72d13294cf8ca4c091&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:17)</a></p>
<p>bind() associates a socket with a local IP address and port number. Hence, P-2.</p>
<p>listen() places a TCP server socket into a passive listening state so that it can wait for incoming connection requests. Hence, Q-3.</p>
<p>accept() accepts a pending incoming connection request and creates a socket for communication with that client. Hence, R-4.</p>
<p>connect() is used by a client to initiate a connection with a remote server. Hence, S-1.</p>
<p>Therefore, the correct matching is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Q</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">S</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, which corresponds to option (D).</p>`
