      answer: "D",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4f7903ac1a2e38d1834b7&questionId=6abfed72d13294cf8ca4c167&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4f7903ac1a2e38d1834b7&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6abfed72d13294cf8ca4c167&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fc24c4772-59d7-4654-b562-8aed3e068f85%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6abfed72d13294cf8ca4c168&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:01:37)</a></p>
<p>Step 1: Check conflict serializability<br /><br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>occurs</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>before</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak="newline"/><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>occurs</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>before</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak="newline"/><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>occurs</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>before</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">W</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>So the precedence graph contains:<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p>
<p>This is a <strong class="x7amdea">cycle</strong>, so the schedule is <strong class="x7amdea">not conflict serializable</strong>.</p>
<p>Step 2: Check view serializability</p>
<p>The final writes are:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak="newline"/><mi mathvariant="normal">y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak="newline"/><mi mathvariant="normal">z</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn></math></p>
<p>Also, T3 reads x from T2's write. Therefore, for view equivalence, T2 must precede T3.</p>
<p>But because the final write on y is by T2, while T3 writes y before T2, view equivalence would require T3 to precede T2.</p>
<p>Thus we get contradictory ordering requirements:<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">T</mi><mn>2</mn></math></p>
<p>So it is not view serializable either.</p>`
