      text: `<p style="text-align: justify;">Consider the single precision <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>IEEE</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>754</mn></math> floating point representation which uses 32-bits to store a number. A register R1 which uses the same representation contains a value <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mn>446</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi></math>. Which of the following options denote the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>*</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math> in single precision <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>IEEE</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>754</mn></math> floating point representation?</p>`,
