      text: `<p>Which of the following statements is/are not incorrect regarding the deadlock, where the system can have multiple processes and each resource having single instance?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>If two processes can use a resource simultaneously then deadlock may occur</p>`,
        `<p>If two processes requested for same resource, then deadlock will surely occur</p>`,
        `<p>If two processes not willing to release their resources, then deadlock can occur</p>`,
        `<p>If two processes are not directly waiting for each other&rsquo;s resources, then the system is not suffering from deadlock&nbsp;</p>`,
      ],
      answer: "C",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4fd7b8180c1555cab3854&questionId=6ac9b9be358b96dc996d63b0&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4fd7b8180c1555cab3854&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6ac9b9be358b96dc996d63b0&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Ffc8e39ef-37ec-476d-8c6c-1c64c472eaf3%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6ac9b9be358b96dc996d63b1&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:05:40)</a></p>
<p><strong>(A) Incorrect: </strong>If 2 processes can share resource then mutual exclusion will not hold for the resource hence no deadlock at all</p>
<p><strong>(B) Incorrect. </strong>Two processes requesting the same resource does not guarantee deadlock. One gets it, uses it, releases it, and the other then proceeds. Deadlock needs all four conditions together, including circular wait.</p>
<p><strong>(C) Correct: </strong>If 2 processes hold their resources then others will wait hence possibility of deadlock is there.</p>
<p><strong>(D) Incorrect:</strong> If 2 processes are not waiting for each other then they may wait for other&rsquo;s resources. Hence deadlock may occur</p>`
