      text: `<p>Let f: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></math> and g: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>be functions. Which of the following statements is NOT necessarily true?</p>`,
