<p id="p-rc_8df48a1d926bcf0c-91" data-path-to-node="43,3,0">Step 4: Evaluate <span class="math-inline" data-math="f(x)" data-index-in-node="17">f(x)</span>&nbsp;at the interval endpoints (<span class="math-inline" data-math="x=-1" data-index-in-node="49"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span class="math-inline" data-math="x=4" data-index-in-node="58"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>)<response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><source-footnote _nghost-ng-c804304336="" class="ng-star-inserted"></source-footnote></response-element>:<sources-carousel-inline ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER" _nghost-ng-c3358956695=""> <source-inline-chip _ngcontent-ng-c3358956695="" _nghost-ng-c4097993517="" class="ng-star-inserted"></source-inline-chip></sources-carousel-inline></p>
