      text: `<p>Consider the following graph G</p>
<p><img title="Screenshot 2026-10-15 213206.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/dfb491d4-9c80-4bb0-a9f7-f3594c0abc4c.png" alt="" width="283" height="221" /></p>
<p>Using the given graph, perform a Depth-First Search (DFS) starting at vertex A and visiting neighbour&rsquo;s in lexicographical order. The no of back edges are present in this traversal is ______________.</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 4,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4fe6de5b979df2433b957&questionId=6ad2149e63f65db1842952fc&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4fe6de5b979df2433b957&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6ad2149e63f65db1842952fc&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F7dedfdf0-527a-451b-a2c5-45c196be6d92%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6ad2149e63f65db1842952fd&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:30)</a></p>
<p>In an undirected graph, DFS has only tree edges and back edges, with no cross or forward edges. So the count doesn&rsquo;t depend on which edges are which:</p>
<ul>
<li>Tree edges = V &minus; 1 = 10 &minus; 1 = 9, provided the graph is connected so DFS from A reaches every vertex.</li>
<li>Back edges = total edges &minus; tree edges = 13 &minus; 9 = <strong>4</strong>.</li>
</ul>`
