      text: `<p>With the given set of keys <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>66</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> a binary search tree is constructed not necessarily in the given order. Which of the following is true?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>A binary search tree with minimum height 2 is possible.</p>`,
        `<p>A binary search tree with minimum height 3 is possible.</p>`,
        `<p>A binary search tree with maximum height 7 is possible.</p>`,
        `<p>A BST with height 7 is possible only if values are inserted in increasing order.</p>`,
      ],
      answer: ["B", "C"],
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4fe6de5b979df2433b957&questionId=6ad2149e63f65db1842953e3&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4fe6de5b979df2433b957&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6ad2149e63f65db1842953e3&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F56e660ab-8436-40b5-9ac0-d46f1d95c37f%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6ad2149e63f65db1842953e4&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:26)</a></p>
<p>Height 3 is possible for the following sequence</p>
<p><img title="1.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/73a21541-5507-4426-a9bc-dac493600035.png" alt="" width="408" height="208" /></p>
<p>Since the order does not matter hence we can create skewed binary tree.</p>
<p><img title="2.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/979e7e47-f173-4dee-9633-e9bf0f14e29e.png" alt="" width="287" height="265" /></p>
<p>(D) is not true because we can also have left skewed binary tree (A) is false: 8 nodes cannot fit in height 2 (max 7 nodes), so minimum height is 3, hence (B) is true. (C) is true: a skewed tree of 8 nodes has height 7.</p>`
