      text: `<p>Consider the following three address code instruction<br />1.&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />2.&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></math><br />3.&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>*</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi></math><br />4.&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />5.&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>*</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />6.&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></math><br />7.&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>if</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>goto</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br />8.&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />9.&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>*</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">k</mi></math><br />10.&nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>]</mo></math><br />11. <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>If</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">b</mi></math> goto (9)<br />12. <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />Number of maximum statement in one basic blocks present in the above three address code is_____.</p>`,
