      answer: 2,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4fe6de5b979df2433b957&questionId=6ad2149e63f65db1842953d7&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4fe6de5b979df2433b957&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6ad2149e63f65db1842953d7&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fa3b271ff-b804-42a9-a8c5-476ded26349e%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6ad2149e63f65db1842953d8&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:10:49)</a></p>
<p>1. <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><msup><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math><br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;From Z: get P, Х.<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;With C, P: CP <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math></span> BQ add B, Q.<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;With B, C: BC <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>AR add A, R.<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;With A, P: AP <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math></span> XYB <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> </span>(adds Y; X, B are already present).</p>
<p>Closure = all attributes<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> {C, Z} is a key.<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>Minimal</mi><mo>:</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><msup><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><msup><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext></math>So neither is a superkey.<br /><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><msup><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math><br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;From Z: get P, Х.<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;From Q, R: QR <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> C.<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;With C, P: CP<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>BQ add <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> </span>B (and Q already present).<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;With B, C: BC<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> AR <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> </span>add A, R (R already present).<br />&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp;With A, P: AP <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> XYB <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> </span>(adds Y).<br />Closure = all attributes <span style="font-family: symbol;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math></span> <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&#160;</mtext></math>is a key.<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Minimal: any 2-element subset <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mfenced><mrow><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mfenced open="{" close="}"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mo>{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Z</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&#160;</mtext></math>fails to reach all attributes.<br />So, there are exactly two candidate keys: CZ and QRZ.</p>`
