      text: `<p style="text-align: justify;">Every host in an IPv4 network has a battery-backed real-time clock with a resolution of 1 second. Each host may generate at most 1000 unique identifiers in one second, and every host has a globally unique 32-bit IPv4 address. A globally unique identifier must contain exactly 50 bits and must distinguish all identifiers generated by a host across different seconds. If the remaining bits are used to identify an identifier within a particular second, after how many seconds will the identifiers generated by a host repeat?</p>`,
