      text: `<p>Six classmates A, B, C, D, E and F are participating in a quiz competition. They are seated in two rows of three members each, facing each other such that each participant in one row sits directly opposite a participant in the other row. Further it is known that D is not seated at either end of a row and sits to the right of E, who faces C. F sits to the left of B, who faces D. Based on the given information, which of the following groups of friends are seated in the same row?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>AEF</p>`,
        `<p>BDE</p>`,
        `<p>CBF</p>`,
        `<p>ABD</p>`,
      ],
      answer: "C",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&questionId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57214de&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57214de&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fbe4ad8c6-dd0d-4e3b-9d62-487c5145c853%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57214df&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:03:01)</a></p>
<p>There are 2 rows, each with 3 people, and every participant faces someone directly opposite.</p>
<p>D is not at either end and is to the right of E (so D must be in the middle position of their row, E is left of D).</p>
<p>E faces C.</p>
<p>F sits to the left of B, who faces D.</p>
<p><img title="10.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/8d05ea80-a2d8-4976-b5a1-6bd1658cac07.png" alt="" width="137" height="105" /></p>`
