      answer: "C",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&questionId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57214e1&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57214e1&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fa082b82c-0cb5-4e3b-b1fe-9039211126d2%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57214e2&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:04:10)</a></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Explanation:</strong> A criterion is a specific principle, rule, or standard by which something is judged or decided. (Note: "Criteria" is the plural form).</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Why others are incorrect: </strong>(A) Paradigm is a typical pattern or model of something. (B) Axiom is a statement that is established, accepted, or self-evidently true. (D) Postulate is a fundamental assumption suggested as a basis for reasoning.</p>`
