      answer: 0,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&questionId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721561&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721561&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F76d6e1c5-5a36-4d5e-96fb-6a3b31ed8d6f%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721562&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:06:05)</a></p>
<p>Total allocated instances of resources:</p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">P</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>
<p>Total available instances =&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>total</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>allocated</mi></math></p>
<p>Available instance of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p>Available instance of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p>Available instance of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">R</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p>Now we will check if any request can be satisfied:</p>
<ul>
<li>P1 requested for 1 instance of R2 cannot be satisfied as instance of any R2 is not available</li>
<li>P2 requested for 1 instance of R3 cannot be satisfied as instance of any R3 is not available</li>
<li>P3 requested for 1 instance of R1 cannot be satisfied as instance of any R1 is not available</li>
<li>P4 requested for 1 instance of R2 cannot be satisfied as instance of any R2 is not available</li>
</ul>
<p>Which means all the processes will have to wait. Which means all the processes are deadlocked. Hence 0 processes can complete the execution without entering into deadlock.</p>`
