      text: `<p><span data-path-to-node="11,0">A n-ary tree is a tree in which each node has n children or no children</span><response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><source-footnote _nghost-ng-c46153305="" class="ng-star-inserted"></source-footnote></response-element><span data-path-to-node="11,2">. Let I be the number of internal nodes and L be the number of leaves in a complete n-ary tree</span><response-element class="no-md" ng-version="0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER"><source-footnote _nghost-ng-c46153305="" class="ng-star-inserted"></source-footnote></response-element><span data-path-to-node="11,4">. If <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>81</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, what is the value of n?</span></p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 9,
