      text: `<p>In a B-Tree, the block size is 512 bytes, search key size is 2 bytes, block pointer size is 6 bytes, and record pointer size is 8 bytes. Every node contains (n - 1) record pointers, (n - 1) search keys, and n block pointers.<br />What is the maximum number of search keys that can be accommodated at level 0 of the B-Tree? (Root is at level 0.)</p>`,
