      text: `<p>Consider the following process scenario with 4 processes P1, P2, P3 and P4. The processes are executed on a single CPU system.</p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 18.2668%; height: 103px;" border="1">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="width: 33.2108%;"><strong>Process</strong></td>
<td style="width: 66.4216%;"><strong>Burst Time</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 33.2108%;">P1</td>
<td style="width: 66.4216%;">4</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 33.2108%;">P2</td>
<td style="width: 66.4216%;">2</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 33.2108%;">P3</td>
<td style="width: 66.4216%;">5</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="width: 33.2108%;">P4</td>
<td style="width: 66.4216%;">1</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The processes executed using pre-emptive SRTF (Shortest Remaining Time First) algorithm. And the execution of the processes is as follows:</p>
<p><img title="WhatsApp Image 2026-10-22 at 1.15.05 PM.jpeg" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/53e24de7-9c73-44a0-8e33-4293997823da.jpeg" alt="" width="521" height="50" /></p>
<p>The Arrival time of each process can be:</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>P1: 0, P2: 0, P3: 2, P4: 4</p>`,
        `<p>P1: 0, P2: 1, P3: 2, P4: 3</p>`,
        `<p>P1: 0, P2: 1, P3: 2, P4: 4</p>`,
        `<p>P1: 0, P2: 1, P3: 6, P4: 4</p>`,
      ],
      answer: ["C", "D"],
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&questionId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721607&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721607&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F744b9000-7faa-4a29-a987-a644ce555759%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721608&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:08:30)</a></p>
<p>In Gantt chart if we check, at time 0 there is only 1 process available P1. Hence the process P1 runs from 0 to 1 then pre-empted which means at 1 P2 (burst time smaller than P1) should arrive then only P1 will be pre-empted. Also after completion of P2 at time 3. P3 can not run because it is biggest process. Hence P1 runs. Now at time 4 P4 arrives and gets the CPU immediately as it is smallest process. Hence arrival time of P4 is 4. P3 can have arrival time from 0 to 7 anything. As it will run only after all processes will complete because it is biggest process.</p>`
