      text: `<p>Two processes P1 and P2 need to access a critical section. Consider the following construct used by both the processes:</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td width="312">
<p><strong>Process P1</strong></p>
</td>
<td width="312">
<p><strong>Process P2</strong></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td width="312">
<p>while(True)</p>
<p>{</p>
<p>&nbsp; Flag1 = False;</p>
<p>&nbsp; while(Flag2 == False)</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp; {</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; //critical section</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Flag1 = True;</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp; }</p>
<p>}</p>
</td>
<td width="312">
<p>while(True)</p>
<p>{</p>
<p>&nbsp; Flag2 = False;</p>
<p>&nbsp; while(Flag1 == False)</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp; {</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; //critical section</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Flag2 = True;</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp; }</p>
<p>}</p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Here Flag1 and Flag2 are Boolean variables shared between both processes, and both are initialized to True. Which of the following statements is/are true?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
        `<p>The given solution fails to guarantee mutual exclusion</p>`,
        `<p>The given solution fails to prevent deadlock</p>`,
        `<p>In the given solution P1 and P2 never starves for critical section</p>`,
        `<p>The given solution prevents deadlock and also guarantees mutual exclusion&nbsp;</p>`,
      ],
      answer: "A",
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&questionId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721665&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721665&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2F8abfe415-7ed7-478b-9a3b-92c0172ceb2c%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6adc905010d0e2cbf5721666&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:07:48)</a></p>
<p>(A)&nbsp; Correct: When both processes set Flag1 and Flag2 to false then for both processes while condition will be true and critical section is inside loop, hence both processes can enter into critical section</p>
<p>(B)&nbsp; Incorrect: Both processes will never have situation where both processes can stuck into deadlock.</p>
<p>(C)&nbsp; Incorrect: If only one process P1 tries to enter into critical section when P2 doesn&rsquo;t arrive, then Flag2 will be true only. Hence P1 will not be able to enter into critical section and will starve in the while(True) loop. Similarly P2 also can starve</p>
<p>(D)&nbsp; Incorrect: As already discussed in option A and B</p>`
