      text: `<p style="text-align: justify;">Consider a hypothetical processor which supports 60 distinct instructions and 12 distinct addressing modes. Each of the instructions consist an opcode, two addressing mode fields and two floating point operand register fields. There are 16 floating point registers and each register can store 32-bits single precision IEEE-754 floating point number. The length of each instruction in processor is _______ bits?</p>`,
      image: "",
      options: [
      ],
      answer: 22,
      solution: `<p><a href="https://www.pw.live/watch/?type=penpencilvdo&mode=public-feeds&cameFrom=test-series&testId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&questionId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57216ee&batchId=&testCategoryId=&parentId=6960b6755c7508c1bb165ed9&childId=69f4ff30e5b979df2433b9ae&vType=TEST_SERIES_QUESTION&secondaryChildId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57216ee&secondaryParentId=undefined&src=https%3A%2F%2Fd1d34p8vz63oiq.cloudfront.net%2Fd18189a4-99d3-45ec-82bf-c4da85b0c931%2Fmaster.mpd&is_comments_enabled=false&is_report_enabled=true&is_rating_enabled=true&is_products_enabled=false&is_header_enabled=true&typeKey=BATCH_QUIZ_VIDEO_SOLUTION&reportTypeKey=questionId&typeId=6adc905010d0e2cbf57216ef&back_button=false" target="_blank" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:8px 16px;background:#5a4bda;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:14px;margin:8px 0;">▶ Watch Video Solution (00:03:30)</a></p>
<p>Number of instructions supported = 60, hence opcode = 6 bits</p>
<p>Number of addressing modes = 12, hence each mode field = 4 bits</p>
<p>Number of floating point registers = 16, hence each register field = 4 bits</p>
<p>Instruction format will be as follows:</p>
<p><img title="5.png" src="https://static.pw.live/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/QBG/e681cfbc-72db-428e-9993-72727cc66df2.png" alt="" width="543" height="57" /></p>
<p>Total instruction length =<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math> bits</p>`
